ASYNCHRONOUS EXECUTION

Asynchronous execution means code does not wait for a long operation to finish.
Time-consuming tasks are handled in the background while the program continues running.

Key points:

* Non-blocking execution
* Improves performance and responsiveness
* Used for tasks like API calls, timers, file handling
* Execution order is not strictly sequential

Example behavior:
Start
End
Async Task

The async task runs later, even if written earlier.

this code will first run the settimeout things then after that get runed it will run the normal things, 
function func1(callback) {
    setTimeout(() => {
        console.log("setTimeout");
        callback()
    }, 10000);
}

function func2() {
    console.log("task 1 ");
    console.log("task 2 ");
    console.log("task 3 ");
}

func1(func2);

